# Nothing in this repository redistributes a game that is still under copyright.
#
# Two kinds of file are therefore never committed:
#
#   original/    the game exactly as it shipped
#   recovered/   a reconstruction that assembles or compiles to a byte-identical
#                copy of it — legally the same thing as the binary, just in
#                source form, and easy to forget for exactly that reason
#
# Every game folder follows this convention, so the rule is one pattern each.
# Everything else — the documentation, the port, the artwork — is our own work
# and is committed normally.
#
# Each game's README explains how to regenerate its recovered/ folder from a
# copy of the game you already own.

*/original/
*/recovered/

# Belt and braces: never commit a DOS executable from anywhere in the tree.
*.com
*.exe
*.COM
*.EXE

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
